\f1\fs22 Alexander, his bravado swollen by his mother\'92s unceasing support, barely acknowledged Chanta, stricken and terrified\'97perhaps a glance; maybe the wry, triumphant curl of his lip was all the confirmation he\'92d afford Chanta. The sneer told him everything:
\f2\i  I\'92ve won Sarah, and you\'92ve lost
\f1\i0 . For a moment, out the limo window, Sarah looked through him with vague eyes, like a ghost from a mirror. Losing Sarah was like a shard shearing away from the flint of Chanta\'92s soul. He felt raw; something inside bled like crushed beetroot. The centimetres between them stretched as the cavalcade eased down the drive and disappeared from sight.\
