\cf2 Chanta fell to his knees and wept. With great reverence, a group of Elvi guided him to his feet, out of the dust, and for a time he let himself go limp beneath their guidance, until a flicker of resolve surfaced somewhere between the ache behind his eyes, the grind of his jaw, and the hollow in his belly. He shook free of their hands and, legs heavy as iron, wandered into the ruins of the mansion.\
