\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Chanta did not leave for days. He sat at the top of what remained of the stairs, swinging his legs over the void where Sarah\'92s room had been. He spoke little, and when he did, his voice was a hollow moan; he considered it a blessing whenever tears would come. Those who took shifts watching over him could never tell if he slept. The sandwiches they set by his side barely lost a corner; he drank almost nothing. Pairs of Dr John and Dr Nick would come and try to persuade him to take some small white tablet or dose. Occasionally, they decided an injection was required, only to be pushed back by other Elvi with thin, set lips and emphatic shakes of the head.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

