\f1\fs22 On the last line, Chanta\'92s voice was joined by a choir of Elvi. They cheered; many wept. One began to snap a rhythm, another found the tempo, and soon the few who had arrived first had taught it to the crowd. They sang in chorus, voices high and keening.\
With each repetition, more joined\'97every guitar was found and strummed, each voice raised. When the singing faded, they sat with the silence.\
The Elvi wept and embraced.\
Shedding tears, Chanta laughed, feeling the bind of grief loosen, if just a little. He wiped his sleeve across his cheek and whispered to no one in particular, \'93I could really go a cheeseburger.\'94
